{
  "_comment": [
    "Industry profiles: what a good website looks like differs by industry, so the audit adapts to it.",
    "",
    "A scan detects the site's industry from its own pages (detect: words on the homepage and in page",
    "titles, URL paths, and structured-data types) or takes it from the scan request. The profile then sets:",
    "  platforms        review / profile / community sites for the off-page checks (OFF-03, OFF-05/06, OFF-07).",
    "                   These REPLACE the default lists; a region chosen for the scan still adds its sites.",
    "                   An empty list means the channel does not apply to the industry.",
    "  content_rubric   what a complete key page covers (ON-10), with keywords for the no-AI fallback.",
    "  page_schema      structured-data types accepted on the industry's key pages (TECH-17).",
    "",
    "`general` is used when no industry is clearly indicated. Edit this file to tune detection, add an",
    "industry or change a list; no code change is needed. INDUSTRY_PROFILES_PATH points at a different file."
  ],
  "detection": {
    "_what": "A profile is chosen when it collects at least min_signals and beats the runner-up by margin x; otherwise `general`.",
    "min_signals": 4,
    "margin": 1.5
  },
  "profiles": {
